{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01331",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.84,
      "end_seconds": 6.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.21,
      "end_seconds": 12.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.96,
      "end_seconds": 28.54,
      "duration_seconds": 15.58,
      "text": "I wanted to get sudden low back pain looked at. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.14,
      "end_seconds": 32.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.5,
      "end_seconds": 38.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I've, I've had it since this morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.3,
      "end_seconds": 50.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "I follow. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.46,
      "end_seconds": 59.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "mm, yes, bending that makes it worse i'd say a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.57,
      "end_seconds": 62.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.7,
      "end_seconds": 73.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "It, It usually comes with a twinge down the thigh. About twinge down the thigh, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.72,
      "end_seconds": 79.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "right, have you noticed leg weakness, fever or numbness in the groin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.73,
      "end_seconds": 83.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.82,
      "end_seconds": 86.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "What about bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.58,
      "end_seconds": 91.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "no, I haven't had any bladder problems"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.78,
      "end_seconds": 99.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.61,
      "end_seconds": 103.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.47,
      "end_seconds": 110.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "alright, have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.6,
      "end_seconds": 115.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "ah, no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.83,
      "end_seconds": 120.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.61,
      "end_seconds": 136.8,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "I, I had an operation for a hernia last spring work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.87,
      "end_seconds": 142.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.52,
      "end_seconds": 157.97,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.88,
      "end_seconds": 163.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.33,
      "end_seconds": 167.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "It's simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.55,
      "end_seconds": 172.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.02,
      "end_seconds": 178.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "For six months. It's paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.19,
      "end_seconds": 181.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.62,
      "end_seconds": 185.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "About three months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.84,
      "end_seconds": 201.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Alright, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.41,
      "end_seconds": 210.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.58,
      "end_seconds": 215.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.2,
      "end_seconds": 219.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.71,
      "end_seconds": 226.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.67,
      "end_seconds": 231.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Let me think, my father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.51,
      "end_seconds": 245.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.94,
      "end_seconds": 261.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Okay, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.36,
      "end_seconds": 289.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "okay: temperature is 36.7 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air. And blood pressure 110 over 81, pulse is 74 beats a minute"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.12,
      "end_seconds": 292.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.22,
      "end_seconds": 296.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.58,
      "end_seconds": 304.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.42,
      "end_seconds": 309.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.51,
      "end_seconds": 324.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "The muscles beside the spine are tight and tender and you can lift both legs fully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.4,
      "end_seconds": 326.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.34,
      "end_seconds": 340.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? It points towards mechanical low back pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.19,
      "end_seconds": 347.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "I mean, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.75,
      "end_seconds": 367.12,
      "duration_seconds": 18.37,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's mechanical low back pain, and we'll watch how it goes. Just to be sure I understood. You've had sudden low back pain, since this morning, and no leg weakness or bladder problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.69,
      "end_seconds": 369.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.24,
      "end_seconds": 398.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "Let's use naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, five days. You take it by mouth. That's for back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.22,
      "end_seconds": 404.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Should I carry on if I feel better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.76,
      "end_seconds": 412.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Please come and and see me if it is not better in two weeks. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.31,
      "end_seconds": 418.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}